From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:04:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/common/cse: No warning for a HECI1 disabled before
 S3

With the ME in soft temporary disable, or with the
disable_heci1_at_pre_boot option, the end of the boot disables HECI1.
On an S3 resume the device is still disabled, the PCI enumeration
disables it in the device tree, and dump_me_status() at the end of
BS_OS_RESUME_CHECK warns "HECI: CSE device 16.0 is disabled" on every
resume, for the state that the boot before the suspend chose.

On resume, when the device of HECI1 is disabled, say why there is no
ME status at the debug level instead.

TEST=On a Lenovo ThinkCentre M920x with the ME in soft temporary
disable, the ramstage of an S3 resume has no warning, and a normal
boot still reports the ME status.

Change-Id: I06dbfdb8c605ee3366ccb370bd550d192dd8d541
---
 src/soc/intel/common/block/cse/cse_spec.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/cse/cse_spec.c b/src/soc/intel/common/block/cse/cse_spec.c
index af64255514d..d5fd9350220 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/cse/cse_spec.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/cse/cse_spec.c
@@ -1,9 +1,12 @@
 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
 
+#include <acpi/acpi.h>
 #include <bootstate.h>
+#include <device/device.h>
 #include <intelblocks/cse.h>
 #include <intelblocks/me.h>
 #include <console/console.h>
+#include <soc/pci_devs.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 
 /*
@@ -39,6 +42,17 @@ static void dump_me_status(void *unused)
 	union me_hfsts6 hfsts6;
 	bool manufacturing_mode;
 
+	/*
+	 * HECI1 disabled at the end of the boot before an S3 suspend (the
+	 * disable_heci1_at_pre_boot option, or the ME in soft temporary disable)
+	 * stays disabled on resume, and the enumeration disables its device:
+	 * the expected state, not a warning.
+	 */
+	if (acpi_is_wakeup_s3() && !is_devfn_enabled(PCH_DEVFN_CSE)) {
+		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "ME: HECI1 disabled before the suspend, no status\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (!is_cse_enabled())
 		return;
 
